{
 "name": "bojophlebia",
 "description": "Bojophlebia prokopi, giant Carboniferous winged insect (early relative of mayflies/dragonflies), top view like a pinned specimen, heading up-right (body tilted 20 degrees like meganeura): four broad, rounded, nearly equal smoky grey-brown wings (#d8d0bc) with darker cross-veins and darker bases, stout dark brown segmented body, short head with two small dark eyes and short antennae, two long thin tail filaments (cerci). No face. Anchor = thorax centre. ~420 wingspan (x -210..210, y -150..175). Greys well with ink #4a4a4a for the fossil slab.",
